      {
        "title": "Loading the Dataset",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Open Statistics Studio and go to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "1. Data",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Upload "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "RT_PatientOutcomes_Sample.csv"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " directly \u2014 no import wizard, no manual variable type declarations."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "One real prep step remains:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " for the Chi-Square analysis later, you'll need "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Satisfaction_Score",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (1\u20135) collapsed into a two-level "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "High/Low",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " category. Do this in a spreadsheet "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "before",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " uploading \u2014 add a column with a formula like "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "=IF(Satisfaction_Score>=4,\"High\",\"Low\")",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "code"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ", save, then upload. This is a completely standard data-prep step in any real research workflow, not something unique to SPSS."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Analysis 1 \u2014 Descriptive Statistics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Go to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "2. Descriptive",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Select "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Age",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", run it, record the mean and SD. Repeat for "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Anxiety_Pre",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Anxiety_Post",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Setup_Error_mm",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Fractions_Completed",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "For "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Treatment_Site",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sex",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", go to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "3. Frequencies",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " instead \u2014 these are categorical, so you want counts and percentages per category, not a mean."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every published study opens with this step: describe your sample before testing anything."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Analysis 2 \u2014 Paired-Samples t-Test (Tests H1)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Go to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "4. Group Tests",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2192 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Paired-samples t test",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Set "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Anxiety_Pre",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as the first variable and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Anxiety_Post",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as the second. Run it."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Same 50 patients, measured twice \u2014 that's what makes this "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "paired",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " rather than independent. Record the mean difference, t, df, p, and the 95% confidence interval directly from the results card."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why is a paired t-test the correct choice for comparing Anxiety_Pre to Anxiety_Post?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Because there are more than two groups",
              "Because the same patients were measured at both time points"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Pairing accounts for each patient's own baseline, which is only valid when the same subjects are measured twice."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Analysis 3 \u2014 One-Way ANOVA (Tests H2)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Still in "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "4. Group Tests",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", find the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "One-way ANOVA",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " card. Set "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Treatment_Site",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as the group variable and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Setup_Error_mm",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as the numeric outcome. Run it."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "One real difference from SPSS:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " Statistics Studio's post-hoc pairwise comparisons use a "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Bonferroni correction",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " rather than Tukey HSD. Both control for the fact that testing multiple pairs inflates your false-positive risk \u2014 Bonferroni is simply a more conservative, more transparent method to compute by hand or in open-source code. Your conclusions (which pairs differ) will typically match; the exact p-values will not match an SPSS Tukey table digit-for-digit."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Record the F statistic, both degrees of freedom, p, and \u03b7\u00b2 from the ANOVA table, then the three pairwise comparisons from the post-hoc table."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Analysis 4 \u2014 Chi-Square Test (Tests H3)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Go to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "6. Categorical",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Set "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Education_Received",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as the row variable and your recoded "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sat_HighLow",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " column as the column variable (the one you created in Page 3). Run it."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Check the observed and expected counts table first \u2014 if any expected cell count is below 5, that's a real limitation to report, not something to ignore."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page7_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "If an expected cell count in your chi-square table is below 5, what should you do?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Report it as a limitation of the chi-square assumption",
              "Ignore it since the test still ran"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Expected counts below 5 violate a key chi-square assumption and should be explicitly noted as a limitation."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Analysis 5 \u2014 Pearson Correlation (Tests H4)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Go to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "5. Relationships",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2192 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Pearson correlation",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Set "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Therapist_Experience_Yrs",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as X and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Setup_Error_mm",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " as Y. Run it \u2014 Statistics Studio also draws the scatterplot automatically."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Record r, p, direction, and strength (Statistics Studio labels the strength descriptor for you using Cohen's 1988 guidelines \u2014 no need to look it up separately)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Synthesis",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Across your four hypothesis tests (H1\u2013H4), you now have a decision for each: reject or fail to reject the null. Pull those four decisions together and think about which single finding would be most actionable for a radiation therapy department to act on immediately."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Applying this to your own work:",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " which of these five analysis types \u2014 descriptive, paired t, ANOVA, chi-square, or Pearson r \u2014 is most likely to fit a research question you'd want to investigate yourself? That choice comes directly from the variables you'd be measuring and their NOIR level (see the Variables & Measurement lesson)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
